### Working Group Drafts

#### MLS Extensions & MLS Targeted Messages
*Presentation:* [MLS Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mls-mls-slides-00)  
*Presenter:* Raphael Robert

- **MLS Extensions (`draft-ietf-mls-extensions`):**
  - Draft -11 includes structural and mechanical clarifications making previously implicit behaviors explicit.
  - Changes are breaking for current implementations. The working group will wait for implementations (OpenMLS, `mls-rs`) to reach stability and complete interoperability testing before progressing the document.
- **MLS Targeted Messages (`draft-ietf-mls-targeted-messages`):**
  - Draft -02 updated HPKE binding and capability negotiation.
  - **Issue #4 (Scope):** Rohan Mahy proposed allowing targeted messages to target multiple recipients in a single message (similar to Welcome message framing) without adding a ratchet. Currently, multi-recipient delivery requires sending separate targeted messages at the application level.
  - Sean Turner noted that pending pull requests from Mark Atwood will be reviewed before issuing a WGLC, and an explicit poll on Issue #4 will be conducted on the mailing list.

