#### MLS PQ Cipher Suites & Ratchet Tree Options
*Presentation:* [MLS PQ Cipher Suites & Ratchet Tree Options](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mls-mls-pq-cipher-suites-ratchet-tree-options-00)  
*Presenter:* Rohan Mahy

- **Post-Quantum Cipher Suites:**
  - The draft is currently in IETF Last Call (ending December 5) with an IESG Telechat date set for December 17.
  - Recent revisions standardized SHA-2 KDFs, assigned spaced-out cipher suite values, and updated ML-DSA usage text based on feedback from Mark Atwood and Mike Wentworth.
- **Ratchet Tree Options (`draft-ietf-mls-ratchet-tree-options`):**
  - Updates include TLS struct cleanups and wire format registration.
  - To maintain signature consistency between full `GroupInfo` and `partial_group_info` when assembling groups, the `ratchet_tree` extension must be placed as the final extension in `GroupInfo` when partial group info is enabled.
  - Rohan Mahy cautioned against expanding central `MLSMessage` struct enums in extension drafts to avoid protocol versioning and matrix management issues seen in legacy protocols.

