#### MLS Virtual Clients
*Presentation:* [MLS Virtual Clients](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mls-mls-virtual-clients-00)  
*Presenter:* Brendan McMillion

- **Document Updates:**
  - Intended status updated from Informational to Standards Track.
  - Reworked Delivery Service (DS) requirements: DS must route messages to all emulator clients backing a single virtual client. Clients must accept messages originating from their own leaf node (overriding RFC 9420 default rejection behavior).
  - Generation conflicts resulting from concurrent device sends under one virtual client can be mitigated via DS enforcement or short-term message retention/retransmission by clients.
  - Added explicit cross-cipher-suite secret derivation via `import_secret` using `KDF.Extract` and `ExpandWithLabel`. Clients receiving Commit/Update/Welcome messages must verify matching public keys.
- **Open Issues & PRs:**
  - *External Commit Resync:* Clients undergoing a self-remove during an external commit resync must retain group state and re-derive private keys rather than tearing down state per RFC 9420.
  - *Derivation Epochs:* Proposal to restrict derivation of higher-level group secrets to specific derivation epochs (e.g., membership changes). This permits non-derivation epoch states to be purged immediately.
  - Open questions remain regarding whether to mark derivation vs. non-derivation epochs, and whether to mandate a maximum age/time bound on derivation epochs to preserve Forward Secrecy and Post-Compromise Secrecy (PCS).

