### Non-Working Group Drafts & Proposals

#### SlimMLS (Optimized MLS for Large Groups & Post-Quantum)
*Presentation:* [MLS Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mls-mls-slides-00)  
*Presenters:* Raphael Robert, Konrad Kohbrok

- Addresses severe bandwidth and memory overhead when combining large groups (e.g., 100 to 1,000 members) with Post-Quantum (PQ) cipher suites (e.g., ML-KEM-1024, ML-DSA-87), where initial Join/Welcome sizes can reach 10 MB and Commits strain background mobile processing limits.
- **Mechanism:** Replaces full public keys with hash references across the tree. Clients only download full public keys when performing KEM operations on their direct co-path. Additional optimizations include batch-signing key packages and streamlined Commit signatures.
- **Session Polls:**
  - *Have you read the SlimMLS I-D?* — yes: 8, no: 11, no_opinion: 2 (total: 36)
  - *Should the WG adopt the SlimMLS I-D?* — yes: 19, no: 0, no_opinion: 1 (total: 36)

