#### Opportunistic Channels
*Presentation:* [MLS Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mls-mls-slides-00)  
*Presenter:* Konrad Kohbrok

- Provides lightweight pairwise signaling (e.g., delivery receipts, read receipts) between members of a large group without establishing separate 1-to-1 MLS groups or relying on heavy PQ targeted messages.
- Defines a reduced 2-party MLS channel operating without a ratchet tree. Post-Compromise Secrecy (PCS) updates are achieved by injecting Pre-Shared Keys (PSKs) from parent groups using pathless Commits.
- Introduces signatureless MLS Public and Private Messages (relying solely on symmetric MAC protection).
- Rohan Mahy noted this mechanism currently targets 2 specific MLS clients rather than multi-device user accounts (unless combined with virtual clients). Raphael Robert noted that while symmetrically protected channels offer slightly lower guarantees than full signatures, they provide significant security gains over unencrypted receipts common in existing products.

