#### User-Controlled Device Authorization for MLS
*Presentation:* [User-Controlled Device Authorization for MLS (draft-atwood-mls-didwebvh-credential)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-mls-user-controlled-device-authorization-for-mls-draft-atwood-mls-didwebvh-credential-00)  
*Presenter:* Mark Atwood (via Chat/Slides)

- `draft-atwood-mls-didwebvh-credential-00` addresses federated architectures (MIMI) where central Authentication Services authorize devices.
- Defines credentials carrying a `did:webvh` hash-chained signed history of device keys that group members check offline. Device revocations propagate via standard MLS Commits.
- Rohan Mahy questioned log overhead; Mark Atwood clarified logs average ~1.5 KB per entry (capped at 1 MB) and suggested credential-by-reference to reduce repetition across multi-device leaves.

